## Quick Start (Scanner)

```powershell
cd C:\Users\sanketa\Documents\UniversalSecurityScanner
python -m venv .venv
.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
pip install -e .
```

Run web app:

```powershell
python run.py
```

Run CLI scan:

```powershell
python -m universal_security_scanner.cli scan --path "C:\path\to\repo" --format sarif --output report.sarif
```

Auto-bootstrap integrated external tools:

```powershell
python -m universal_security_scanner.cli bootstrap-tools --path "C:\path\to\repo"
```

## Enterprise Coverage Mode (Recommended)

Install external analyzers and keep them available in PATH:

```powershell
# Optional manual install (scanner can also auto-bootstrap)
pip install semgrep
```

Control tool integrations with env vars:

- `USS_USE_EXTERNAL_TOOLS=true|false` (default: true)
- `USS_EXTERNAL_TOOLS=semgrep,trivy,gitleaks,codeql`
- `USS_EXTERNAL_TOOL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=300`
- `USS_AUTO_BOOTSTRAP_TOOLS=true|false` (default: true)
- `USS_TOOLS_DIR=.toolchain`

If tools are missing, scans still run and report warnings instead of failing.

## Dashboard Mock (React)

```powershell
cd frontend\dashboard-mock
npm install
npm run dev
```

## Enterprise Deployment

### Docker Compose

```powershell
docker compose -f deploy\docker\docker-compose.enterprise.yml up --build
```

### Kubernetes (Helm)

```powershell
helm upgrade --install codesentinelx deploy/kubernetes/helm/codesentinelx -n security --create-namespace
```

